course: dictionary
lesson: 15554
title: Supervision
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Supervision means watching over people or work to make sure things are done correctly and safely. A grown-up who gives supervision keeps an eye on what is happening. «The children made toast in the kitchen under adult supervision.» Under supervision means a grown-up or a person in charge is watching.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence. Kitchen, toast and adult tell you that a safe activity is being watched by someone responsible. If you swap in "watching over" for supervision, the sentence still makes sense, so you know you have the right meaning.
explain: Supervision is a noun, a thing you can have. The verb is supervise. «Mr Patel supervises the workers on the building site.» Here Mr Patel is the person in charge, and he is watching over the workers.
fact: Supervision means watching over people or work to make sure things are done correctly and safely.
fact: «Under supervision» means with a grown-up or a person in charge watching.
fact: «Adult supervision» means a grown-up is watching over the activity.
fact: «Without supervision» means nobody in charge is watching.
fact: Activities such as cooking, using tools, swimming and science experiments often need adult supervision.
exercise: «Children must swim under supervision.» What does under supervision mean? | Very quickly | Alone in the deep end | Without any water | *With a grown-up watching over them
exercise: «The manager gives supervision to the new workers.» What is the manager doing? | Playing a game with the workers | Cleaning the office | Going home early | *Watching over the workers to make sure the work is done correctly
exercise: Which activity most needs adult supervision? | Drawing a picture of a tree | *Using sharp tools in a workshop | Reading a book quietly at home | Choosing a song to sing
test:
«The science experiment was done under close supervision.» What does close supervision mean? | *Being watched very carefully | Being left alone to finish | Being given a prize | Being ignored by everyone
«Without supervision, the little ones should not use the oven.» What does without supervision mean? | *With nobody in charge watching | With a grown-up watching closely | With a big smile on their face | With brand new equipment
exam: «Lena cooked pasta with her dad's supervision, so she was safe.» What is supervision in this sentence? | Her dad cooking the pasta for her | Her dad buying the food | *Her dad watching over her to keep her safe | Lena eating the pasta quickly
